      "name": "Suizenji Jojuen Garden",
      "description": "Suizenji Jojuen is a classic Edo-period strolling garden laid out in 1632 by the Hosokawa daimyo clan. The garden features a large central pond with a miniature Mt. Fuji, a recreation of the 53 stations of the Tokaido road, and a traditional teahouse overlooking the serene landscape.",
